      "final_text": "## Setup\n\n8432 in binary is `10000011110000` = 8192 + 128 + 64 + 32 + 16, so\n\n7^8432 = 7^16 \u00b7 7^32 \u00b7 7^64 \u00b7 7^128 \u00b7 7^8192 (mod 5557)\n\n## Repeated squaring of 7 (mod 5557)\n\n| exponent | value |\n|---|---|\n| 7^1 | 7 |\n| 7^2 | 49 |\n| 7^4 | 2401 |\n| 7^8 | 2401\u00b2 = 5,764,801 \u2192 **2192** |\n| 7^16 | 2192\u00b2 = 4,804,864 \u2192 **3616** |\n| 7^32 | 3616\u00b2 = 13,075,456 \u2192 **5392** |\n| 7^64 | 5392\u00b2 = 29,073,664 \u2192 **4997** |\n| 7^128 | 4997\u00b2 = 24,970,009 \u2192 **2408** |\n| 7^256 | 2408\u00b2 = 5,798,464 \u2192 **2513** |\n| 7^512 | 2513\u00b2 = 6,315,169 \u2192 **2417** |\n| 7^1024 | 2417\u00b2 = 5,841,889 \u2192 **1482** |\n| 7^2048 | 1482\u00b2 = 2,196,324 \u2192 **1309** |\n| 7^4096 | 1309\u00b2 = 1,713,481 \u2192 **1925** |\n| 7^8192 | 1925\u00b2 = 3,705,625 \u2192 **4663** |\n\n## Combining the needed factors\n\n- 3616 \u00b7 5392 = 19,497,472 \u2192 3516\n- 3516 \u00b7 4997 = 17,569,452 \u2192 3775\n- 3775 \u00b7 2408 = 9,090,200 \u2192 4505\n- 4505 \u00b7 4663 = 21,006,815 \u2192 1355\n\n(Cross-check: 5557 is prime, so by Fermat the exponent reduces to 8432 mod 5556 = 2876, which gives the same residue.)\n\n**1355**"
